                    briefing_text_r3:       `A mid-design shock: closing the warehouse gap <em>fully now</em> would consume ~40% of the envelope and starve the specialists, the works council demands equal pay for equal work <strong>now</strong>, and managers argue more variable pay for them is “unfair” to frontline staff. Hold the internal-equity ratio <strong>and</strong> defend the specialists via a defensible market-premium rule, justify differential variable pay on a fairness principle, and prepare a works-council position — reserving a concession to trade rather than imposing the design.`,
